{"n": 165, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "165.webp", "text": "12 — 10\n\n1211004 EHECKING AND ADJUSTING\nIGNITION TIMING\n~ 6 Cylinder Models —\n\nCaution!\n\nRefer to page 12 - 0 for instructions when\n\nworking on the engine electrical system.\n\nTesting Conditions:\n\n= Check for correct installed position of\nTDC transmitter to the vibration damper.\nEngine at operating temperature =\noil temperature > 60° C (140° F).\nDistributor/DME control unit numbers* *\nmust agree with specifications on the.\nnominal value microfiche.\n\nConnect BMW service tester or BMW digital\ntester to operating instructions.\n\nModels with NOx Control:\n\n~— The NOx control is integrated in the DME\ncontrol unit of DME engines with NOx\ncontrol,\n\nThe ignition timing at idle speed is not\ninfluenced.\n\n— The NOx control unit is series connected\nwith the ignition control unit as a second\ncontrol unit in case of engines with TCI.\nOperation of the NOx contro! must be\nstopped to chetk the ignition timing.\n\nPull off 4.8 mm (0.189\") plug on the 17°C\n{63° F) temperature switch and connect on\nground..\n\nCheck/adjust ignition timing.\n\nThe ignition timing of cars with NOx control\nwill be retarded by approx. 10° at about\n1500 rpm.\n\n** See Specifications\n\nChecking Owell Angle:\n\nThe dwell angle is given by design and can be\nchecked, but not adjusted\n\nThe DME control unit 1 no longer ready tor\nuse in case of malfunction\n\nCheck ing/Adjusting Ignition Timing* — Cars\nwith Distributor Engine:\n\nPull off vacuum hoses\n\nF = advance ignition control (black)\n\nS = retard ignition control (black/white)\n\nCars with Automatic Transmission:\n\nNo hose for retard ignition control — connection\non vacuum box not used.\n\nImportant!\n\nThe ignition control boxes are inversed on\ndistributors with larger diameter vacuum hose\nconnections — see pictures.\n\nF = advance control (black) (4 mm/0.157” dia.)\nS = retard control (black/red) (8 mm/0.315\" dia.)\n\nDME Engine:\nIgnition timing corrections are not possible.\n\nStart and accelerate engine to test speed”\nCheck ignition timing*, adjusting if necessary.\nCorrect by loosening bolt (1) and turning the\ndistributor on splines (2) accordingly\n\n+°®= ignition timing advanced\n\n— = ignition timing retarded\n\n* See Nominal Value Microfiche", "words": [["12", 0.4661, 0.0192, 0.541, 0.0418], ["—", 0.4975, 0.0166, 0.5091, 0.0517], ["10", 0.5198, 0.0192, 0.541, 0.0418], ["1211004", 0.2604, 0.067, 0.308, 0.0776], ["EHECKING", 0.3212, 0.0676, 0.3789, 0.0789], ["AND", 0.3825, 0.0676, 0.4063, 0.0782], ["ADJUSTING", 0.4103, 0.0676, 0.4732, 0.0796], ["IGNITION", 0.3217, 0.0836, 0.3723, 0.0942], ["TIMING", 0.3769, 0.0836, 0.4164, 0.0948], ["~", 0.3227, 0.1048, 0.3278, 0.1068], ["6", 0.3323, 0.0995, 0.3379, 0.1101], ["Cylinder", 0.3414, 0.0995, 0.382, 0.1121], ["Models", 0.386, 0.1001, 0.4189, 0.1107], ["—", 0.4235, 0.1061, 0.4296, 0.1074], ["Caution!", 0.2584, 0.132, 0.2999, 0.1412], ["Refer", 0.2594, 0.1472, 0.2847, 0.1578], ["to", 0.2893, 0.1499, 0.2989, 0.1585], ["page", 0.3019, 0.1505, 0.3237, 0.1605], ["12", 0.3283, 0.1479, 0.3389, 0.1585], ["-", 0.3414, 0.1446, 0.3455, 0.1638], ["0", 0.3485, 0.1479, 0.3546, 0.1585], ["for", 0.3576, 0.1479, 0.3713, 0.1592], ["instructions", 0.3759, 0.1499, 0.4311, 0.1592], ["when", 0.4347, 0.1485, 0.4595, 0.1592], ["working", 0.2584, 0.1638, 0.2974, 0.1771], ["on", 0.3009, 0.1664, 0.3131, 0.1744], ["the", 0.3171, 0.1645, 0.3318, 0.1744], ["engine", 0.3354, 0.1664, 0.3658, 0.1771], ["electrical", 0.3688, 0.1645, 0.4113, 0.1751], ["system.", 0.4154, 0.1664, 0.4498, 0.1777], ["Testing", 0.2594, 0.1797, 0.2928, 0.1923], ["Conditions:", 0.2969, 0.1797, 0.3526, 0.1903], ["=", 0.2604, 0.2016, 0.2644, 0.2023], ["Check", 0.2705, 0.195, 0.2999, 0.2062], ["for", 0.3045, 0.1956, 0.3176, 0.2062], ["correct", 0.3222, 0.1976, 0.3551, 0.2062], ["installed", 0.3592, 0.1963, 0.3982, 0.2069], ["position", 0.4017, 0.1963, 0.4397, 0.2089], ["of", 0.4438, 0.1963, 0.4529, 0.2069], ["TDC", 